  "bodyText": "“Oops.”\nWomen tried bizarre ways to get his attention, but none worked on him!\n“From her.” \n“Do you know who I am?”\n“A drunkard, I suppose?”\n“You work for me. Remember that.”\n“Actually, I work for the bar. You're just a customer.”\n“You think you're funny?”\n“No. I think you're drunk.”\n“Who is she?”\n“Just a waitress here.”\n“Arrange a meeting for next Thursday, I want to see her again”\nI didn’t realise the Underworld King was sitting across and watching me all along.\nBy the next morning, four of his most dangerous men were standing outside my apartment.\nThe King of the Underworld had already made up his mind.\nHe wanted me.\nI’m fine, Adrik. Thank you for asking. Tired, but fine.\nGood. You should get rest. Put arnica on your bruises – it will help them heal faster. I’m sure by\nnow they’re quite dark.\nYou ain’t joking. My entire neck is purple. I’ll have to go to the store for arnica. I don’t have any.\nI’ll have some sent over. You rest. It will be there when you wake. Good night, Persephone. Adrik wrote.\nThanks. Good night. I said.\nI locked my phone again and put it on my bedside table. I sat on my bed, lost in thought. \nWhy did I suddenly have that warm feeling in my stomach again? Why was the top guy in the mafia checking on me? Why did he send his personal bodyguards to keep an eye on me? What was really going on?\nWhat happened in that meeting while I was out of the room?\n\nHe runs the entire city. She serves tables. So why did he put his four deadliest men outside her door and what is he keeping her alive for? \nTo find out, listen to the free episodes of King of the Underworld, only on Pocket FM",
